<h2 data-section-id=3D"1h63pe8" data-start=3D"235" data-end=3D"275">Portfol=
io Homepage: Mission Statement</h2>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"rpzp6b" data-start=3D"277" data-end=3D"294">Project =
Title</h3>
<p data-start=3D"295" data-end=3D"347"><strong data-start=3D"295" data-end=
=3D"347">SmartSchedule AI: A Student Scheduling Prototype</strong></p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"ag23f6" data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"367">Global C=
ontext</h3>
<p data-start=3D"368" data-end=3D"416"><strong data-start=3D"368" data-end=
=3D"416">Technical Innovation / Education Improvement</strong></p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"176wd6y" data-start=3D"418" data-end=3D"438">Mission=
 Abstract</h3>
<p data-start=3D"439" data-end=3D"1087">My project is a prototype app calle=
d SmartSchedule AI. It is designed to help schools generate student schedul=
es faster and with fewer mistakes. Creating schedules is difficult because =
schools must balance required classes, electives, teacher availability, cla=
ss periods, and class size limits. My prototype uses AI-style logic to orga=
nize these factors and create schedules for students automatically. I chose=
 this project because scheduling is an important school task that affects m=
any students and staff members. This project shows how technology can be us=
ed to solve real school problems and improve efficiency in the Orlando scho=
ol community.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"ij0d9y" data-start=3D"1089" data-end=3D"1108">Framew=
ork Focus</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1109" data-end=3D"1177"><strong data-start=3D"1109" data-e=
nd=3D"1134">Goal 3: Communication</strong><br data-start=3D"1134" data-end=
=3D"1137">
<strong data-start=3D"1137" data-end=3D"1177">Goal 4: Critical &amp; Creati=
ve Thinking</strong></p>
<hr data-start=3D"1179" data-end=3D"1182">
<h1 data-section-id=3D"163ehsg" data-start=3D"1184" data-end=3D"1229">Secti=
on 1: The Process Journal (Goal 1 &amp; 4)</h1>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"s10lgf" data-start=3D"1231" data-end=3D"1259">The Br=
ainstorming Archive</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1260" data-end=3D"1867">At the beginning of this project, =
I knew I wanted to create something with technology and coding. I thought a=
bout problems in schools that affect many people. One problem I focused on =
was student scheduling. Making schedules is complicated because students ne=
ed required classes, electives, and teachers must be available at certain t=
imes. I realized this would be a good challenge because it combines school =
needs with technology. My original big idea was to create a simple applicat=
ion that could take student information and automatically build a schedule =
using rules, almost like a simplified AI system.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"1xs6lm" data-start=3D"1869" data-end=3D"1894">The Ch=
ronological Feed</h2>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71n" data-start=3D"1895" data-end=3D"1905">Week 1=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1906" data-end=3D"2093">I brainstormed project ideas and d=
ecided to focus on a school-related problem. I chose scheduling because it =
is something schools deal with every year and it can be difficult to organi=
ze.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71k" data-start=3D"2095" data-end=3D"2105">Week 2=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2106" data-end=3D"2281">I listed the things my app would n=
eed to consider, such as student name, grade level, required classes, elect=
ive choices, teacher availability, class periods, and seat limits.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71l" data-start=3D"2283" data-end=3D"2293">Week 3=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2294" data-end=3D"2446">I planned the layout of the protot=
ype and decided it should include a way to generate random students and the=
n produce schedules for them automatically.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71q" data-start=3D"2448" data-end=3D"2458">Week 4=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2459" data-end=3D"2600">I started building the prototype c=
ode. I worked on making the app easy to understand and clear enough to show=
 a teacher, not just functional.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71r" data-start=3D"2602" data-end=3D"2612">Week 5=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2613" data-end=3D"2741">I tested the app with multiple stu=
dents and checked whether it could avoid schedule conflicts and place class=
es in open periods.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"mjn71o" data-start=3D"2743" data-end=3D"2753">Week 6=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2754" data-end=3D"2885">I improved the design and added ex=
planation boxes so the app clearly shows the problem, solution, and how the=
 AI-style logic works.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"ybkzyw" data-start=3D"2887" data-end=3D"2905">The Fa=
ilure Log</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"3357">One setback I had was realizing th=
at real school scheduling is much more complicated than I first thought. At=
 first, I imagined the app could just place classes quickly, but I learned =
that schedules depend on many limits and conflicts. My first version was to=
o simple. To fix this, I changed my plan and made a prototype instead of pr=
etending I had built a full real-world system. That helped me focus on maki=
ng one part work clearly and successfully.</p>
