I does not always mean robots or chatbots. It can also mean systems that ma=
ke smart choices based on data and rules.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"ghv9qg" data-start=3D"4503" data-end=3D"4554">4. Sou=
rce about class size or school operations</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4555" data-end=3D"4662"><strong data-start=3D"4555" data-e=
nd=3D"4573">How it helped:</strong> This source helped me see why seat limi=
ts and teacher availability matter in scheduling.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1xp08e5" data-start=3D"4664" data-end=3D"4740">5. In=
terview or conversation with a teacher, counselor, or administrator</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4741" data-end=3D"4895"><strong data-start=3D"4741" data-e=
nd=3D"4759">How it helped:</strong> This primary research helped me connect=
 my idea to a real school setting and understand what adults in schools act=
ually have to manage.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"h9d6hv" data-start=3D"4897" data-end=3D"4925">Primar=
y Research Evidence</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4926" data-end=3D"4978">For this section, you can write so=
mething like this:</p>
<p data-start=3D"4980" data-end=3D"5410">I discussed my project idea with a=
dults and used their feedback to make my prototype more realistic. One impo=
rtant idea I learned was that school scheduling is more complicated than it=
 looks because schools must balance many needs at the same time. I also lea=
rned that a prototype does not need to solve every problem to still show a =
useful idea. This helped me focus on making a clear model instead of an unr=
ealistic full system.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"gkimir" data-start=3D"5412" data-end=3D"5450">Langua=
ge of the Discipline Glossary</h2>
