<p data-start=3D"6028" data-end=3D"6113">Artificial Intelligence (AI) =E2=
=80=94 Technology that makes decisions using data and logic</p>
<p data-start=3D"6115" data-end=3D"6179">Prototype =E2=80=94 An early versi=
on of a product used to test an idea</p>
<p data-start=3D"6181" data-end=3D"6234">Constraint =E2=80=94 A rule or lim=
it the system must follow</p>
<p data-start=3D"6236" data-end=3D"6296">Conflict =E2=80=94 When two classe=
s are scheduled at the same time</p>
<p data-start=3D"6298" data-end=3D"6341">Input =E2=80=94 Information entere=
d into a system</p>
<p data-start=3D"6343" data-end=3D"6385">Output =E2=80=94 The result produc=
ed by a system</p>
<p data-start=3D"6387" data-end=3D"6451">Seat Limit =E2=80=94 The maximum n=
umber of students allowed in a class</p>
<p data-start=3D"6453" data-end=3D"6512">Teacher Availability =E2=80=94 The=
 times when a teacher can teach</p>
<p data-start=3D"6514" data-end=3D"6567">Scheduling Logic =E2=80=94 The rul=
es used to assign classes</p>
<p data-start=3D"6569" data-end=3D"6632">Priority =E2=80=94 Giving certain =
choices more importance than others</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6634" data-end=3D"6637">
<h1 data-section-id=3D"eu6jb3" data-start=3D"6639" data-end=3D"6696">=E2=9C=
=85 SECTION 3: THE PRODUCT / OUTCOME GALLERY (Goal 4 &amp; 5)</h1>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"5863cm" data-start=3D"6698" data-end=3D"6724">The Fi=
nal Masterpiece</h2>
<p data-start=3D"6725" data-end=3D"7195">My final product is a working prot=
otype called SmartSchedule AI. The application generates student schedules =
using AI-style logic. It takes into account required classes, elective choi=
ces, teacher availability, class periods, and class size limits. The system=
 can generate schedules for 10 random students and also create a schedule f=
or a custom student. My goal was to demonstrate how technology can solve a =
real school problem, not to build a full professional system.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"7197" data-end=3D"7200">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"wbzggj" data-start=3D"7202" data-end=3D"7223">Before=
 and After</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7225" data-end=3D"7398"><strong data-start=3D"7225" data-e=
nd=3D"7236">Before:</strong><br data-start=3D"7236" data-end=3D"7239">
Before this project, I thought scheduling was a simple process. I did not r=
ealize how many rules and decisions are involved in building schedules for =
students.</p>
<p data-start=3D"7400" data-end=3D"7635"><strong data-start=3D"7400" data-e=
nd=3D"7410">After:</strong><br data-start=3D"7410" data-end=3D"7413">
After completing this project, I understand that scheduling is a complex sy=
stem that requires balancing many factors. My project shows that technology=
 can help reduce errors, save time, and improve organization in schools.</p=
>
<hr data-start=3D"7637" data-end=3D"7640">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"snwjg0" data-start=3D"7642" data-end=3D"7672">Eviden=
ce of Collaboration</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7673" data-end=3D"7989">I used feedback from adults and my=
 interview with the vice principal to improve my project. This feedback hel=
ped me understand how real scheduling systems work and made my prototype mo=
re realistic. It also helped me focus on building a clear and understandabl=
e solution instead of trying to solve everything at once.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"7991" data-end=3D"7994">
<h1 data-section-id=3D"6hxrrx" data-start=3D"7996" data-end=3D"8016">=E2=9C=
=85 100-WORD SUMMARY</h1>
<p data-start=3D"8018" data-end=3D"8736">SmartSchedule AI is a prototype ap=
plication designed to help schools generate student schedules more efficien=
tly. Creating schedules is a complex process because schools must balance r=
equired classes, electives, teacher availability, class periods, and class =
size limits. My project uses AI-style logic to organize these factors and a=
utomatically generate schedules for students. Through research and an inter=
view with a school administrator, I learned that real scheduling systems al=
so consider student priorities and fairness. This project demonstrates how =
technology can help solve real problems in schools, improve organization, a=
nd reduce errors while showing how AI could support education systems in th=
e future.</p>
